          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-29 23:46:03.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten conf-sanity 103",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten conf-sanity 103\n\nconf-sanity test_103 renames the filesystem three times, each\nfollowed by a full stop and setupall: lustre to mylustre, to\ntfs, and back to lustre. The middle round only repeats the\npool checks on a second name; the rename of an already renamed\nfilesystem is still exercised by the rename back.\n\nDrop the tfs round and run the final pool checks after the\nrename back to the original name. The pools, file and stripe\npool checks are unchanged, and the filesystem is still left\nmounted for the following tests.\n\nOn a test VM, ONLY=103 took 100s, 107s, 100s and 95s before\nand 80s, 66s and 70s after. CI averages 584s over 4433 runs\nper 30 days; removing one of three rename rounds saves about\n28% there, roughly 160s per run, or about 200 hours per 30\ndays.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=103\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I13b4229b79c420de1adfcc6ade31d46e6c13129e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
